  "valuation_insights": "Costco Wholesale Corporation's fiscal 2026 total revenue was reported at $303.154 billion [C:revenue_current], representing a year-over-year growth of 10.14% [C:revenue_growth]. The operating income for the year was $11.685 billion, yielding an operating margin of approximately 3.85% [C:operating_income_current][C:operating_margin]. Net income attributable to the company reached $9.226 billion, supported by a GAAP diluted EPS of $20.76 [C:net_income_current][C:diluted_eps_current]. The company exhibited a strong return on average equity of roughly 28.40%, highlighting efficient equity utilization [C:return_on_average_equity]. Its debt-to-equity ratio remained conservative at 0.172, inclusive of current long-term debt [C:debt_to_equity]. Free cash flow was robust at $9.382 billion, signaling strong cash generation capacity beyond capital expenditures [C:free_cash_flow]. \n\nFor the latest fiscal quarter (16 weeks ended August 30, 2026), net sales increased 11.2% to $93.9 billion compared to the same period last year, indicating positive momentum [C:quarterly_revenue_growth]. The GAAP diluted EPS for this quarter was $6.75 [C:quarterly_diluted_eps]. Given the current stock price of $904.7, the price-to-earnings ratio stands at approximately 43.58, suggesting market optimism or premium valuation [C:price_to_earnings]. \n\nComparing Costco's operating margin of 3.85% with peers—Walmart at 4.18%, Target at 4.88%, and BJ's Wholesale Club at 3.81%—Costco's margin is slightly below Target and Walmart but marginally ahead of BJ's, indicating competitive profitability in the wholesale club retail sector [C:peer_operating_margins]. \n\nInsight: Costco Wholesale Corporation strategically expanded to 939 warehouses globally by fiscal year-end 2026, operating in 15 countries including significant presence in the U.S., Canada, Mexico, Japan, and several European and Asian markets, bolstering its international footprint and e-commerce platforms [L:10-K, line 21].",
